1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,658
A Talk That Changed Direction My first talk was a bore it

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:09,842
sounded elaborate but gave listeners little to use I had mistaken simplicity

3
00:00:09,855 --> 00:00:14,447
for ignorance and filled the slides with vague claims A peer asked

4
00:00:14,461 --> 00:00:20,895
what I actually meant That commonsense question changed the presentation I removed

5
00:00:20,908 --> 00:00:26,605
an improper comparison and explained why one inference was only tentative Inasmuch

6
00:00:26,618 --> 00:00:31,697
as the evidence was incomplete I could not claim certainty Notwithstanding that

7
00:00:31,711 --> 00:00:36,710
limitation the project still offered a useful insight I would not say

8
00:00:36,724 --> 00:00:41,842
the result was incredible or doubtless correct merely to impress I also

9
00:00:41,855 --> 00:00:47,092
replaced male versus female abilities with a more precise question about expectations

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,829
Describing a role as masculine or feminine did not prove that anyone

11
00:00:51,842 --> 00:00:56,882
was naturally suited to it The improved talk avoided an empty opposition

12
00:00:56,895 --> 00:01:01,684
and offered a clear argument Careful wording can help listeners think rather

13
00:01:01,697 --> 00:01:03,513
than simply persuade them to agree
